(5642203, 819915, 100773, '<td valign="top">There''s something wrong in this photo. Wild, WILD guess on what it is: Noise you have added, or that existed in the original shot, disturbed some of the pixels. The edges are a bit strange. Another WILD guess: You added noise before you resized the photo. Applying filters should be done after resizing. If you knew this and I''m terribly wrong, send the dude in the photo after me. If my comment "was helpfull" (which I hope, concidering the choices if it wasn''t), then.... something. SKu looks grat though, could''ve been darker to realy match up her style. You are very close!</td>', 'There''s something wrong in this photo. Wild, WILD guess on what it is: Noise you have added, or that existed in the original shot, disturbed some of the pixels. The edges are a bit strange. Another WILD guess: You added noise before you resized the photo. Applying filters should be done after resizing. If you knew this and I''m terribly wrong, send the dude in the photo after me. If my comment "was helpfull" (which I hope, concidering the choices if it wasn''t), then.... something. SKu looks grat though, could''ve been darker to realy match up her style. You are very close!', '2009-09-09 15:46:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5642208, 819998, 100773, '<td valign="top">I have written comments on almost every entry now, and many of them goes something like this: "I''m having a hard time seeing the relevance". The conversion is good, but in Heidastyle it apears to be a bit "weak". Much more contrast to be a Heida b&amp;w (in my oppinion), or a more desaturated look (play with the saturation slider if you have one in your editing software) and you¨''ll know. The grain in this fits perfectly, it''s just that I''m not sure about the toning.</td>', 'I have written comments on almost every entry now, and many of them goes something like this: "I''m having a hard time seeing the relevance". The conversion is good, but in Heidastyle it apears to be a bit "weak". Much more contrast to be a Heida b&w (in my oppinion), or a more desaturated look (play with the saturation slider if you have one in your editing software) and you¨''ll know. The grain in this fits perfectly, it''s just that I''m not sure about the toning.', '2009-09-09 15:49:13.000000', NULL, 1),
